<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Welcome copy (docs/architecture/ui-ux.md#onboarding): core value proposition,
  a short privacy/local-control reassurance, and one primary action.
  Ordinary language only: no protocol vocabulary, no address, no port.

  Local-network explanation and Discovery copy (S02, Issue #73) follow the same
  rule: no protocol, discovery-mechanism, port or address vocabulary. A test
  (ForbiddenVocabularyTest) enforces it for every localnetwork_ and discovery_
  string.

  Pairing and Remote copy (S03, Issue #79) follow it too, and add the
  television-security vocabulary that may never appear: no port, no certificate,
  no transport name, no token, no protocol generation. Pairing speaks in ordinary
  language about allowing AppT on the television.
-->
<resources>
